          "date": "2026-11-20 15:02:45.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-16518 osd-wbcfs: fix uninitialized result in osd_create_type_f",
        "message": "LU-16518 osd-wbcfs: fix uninitialized result in osd_create_type_f\n\nlbug_with_loc() is only marked __noreturn when objtool knows about\nit (HAVE_LBUG_WITH_LOC_IN_OBJTOOL), so on other kernels the compiler\nassumes LBUG() returns. clang then fails the build with -Werror:\n\n  osd_object.c:533:2: error: variable 'result' is used\n  uninitialized whenever switch default is taken\n  [-Werror,-Wsometimes-uninitialized]\n\nSet result to NULL in the default case of osd_create_type_f().\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 25813cf8ba53 (\"LU-18813 osd-wbcfs: MemFS-based OSD with writeback support\")\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7ff7f852e109fee5c6e96806fffa323f6a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
